@startuml Appendix C Direct Streaming Sequence

!define ASYNC_COLOR #LightBlue
!define SYNC_COLOR #LightCoral
!define STREAM_COLOR #LightGreen
!define EVENT_COLOR #Orange

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

title Appendix C - Direct Streaming Alternative Architecture

actor "User" as user
participant "sim-engine-frontend" as frontend #LightYellow
participant "sim-engine-backend" as backend #23c6b7
queue "Message Broker" as broker #MediumPurple
participant "calculation-engine" as calcEngine #LightGreen
database "Source Database" as sourceDB #LightGray
participant "simulation-engine" as simEngine #23c6b7
database "Simulation DB" as simDB #LightGray

== Simulation Submission ==

user -> frontend: Initiate simulation
frontend -> backend: HTTPS REST\nPOST /simulation
activate backend
backend -> broker: Publish:\n**simulation.requested**
backend --> frontend: HTTP 202 Accepted\n(simulation_id)
deactivate backend

== Direct Streaming Phase ==

broker -> calcEngine: Consume:\n**simulation.requested**
activate calcEngine

calcEngine -> sourceDB: Native DB protocol\nSQL query
activate sourceDB
sourceDB --> calcEngine: Stream result set
deactivate sourceDB

note over calcEngine, simEngine
  **Key Difference:**
  Direct streaming eliminates
  intermediate object storage.
  Uses gRPC streaming or
  Apache Arrow Flight.
end note

calcEngine -> simEngine: gRPC streaming\nor Arrow Flight\n(streamed rows)
activate simEngine

simEngine -> simDB: Bulk load\n(streaming)
activate simDB
simDB --> simEngine: Load progress
deactivate simDB

simEngine -> broker: Publish:\n**persistence.completed**
deactivate simEngine

calcEngine -> broker: Publish:\n**calculation.completed**
deactivate calcEngine

== Status Update ==

broker -> backend: Consume:\n**completion events**
activate backend
backend --> frontend: Job status update
deactivate backend

frontend --> user: Display results

note over frontend, simDB
  **Benefits:**
  - No intermediate storage needed
  - Lower latency (direct transfer)
  - Reduced storage costs

  **Tradeoffs:**
  - Tighter coupling between services
  - Requires stable network connection
  - Less resilience to failures
end note

@enduml

